cfPDFPagesFP: flush the temporary PDF before PDFio opens it

cfPDFPagesFP() copies its input to a temporary file through stdio and
then hands the file name to pdfioFileOpen() without flushing. The
unwritten tail can hold the cross-reference table and trailer, so the
page count fails with "Missing Root object" / "Unexpected page count"
and PDF-to-raster / PDF-to-PCL-XL jobs stop with "universal filter
failed".

Backport of OpenPrinting/libcupsfilters#167 (e14bad4), reduced to its
functional fflush(). Also carried by projectbluefin/dakota#1724 in the
SDK patch queue; drop when the base's libcupsfilters has it (see the
Containerfile's libcupsfilters-builder).

--- a/cupsfilters/pdf.c
+++ b/cupsfilters/pdf.c
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@
     fwrite(buffer, 1, bytes_read, temp_fp);
   }
 
+  fflush(temp_fp);
   // Open the temp file with pdfio
   pdfio_file_t *pdf = pdfioFileOpen(temp_filename, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
 
